Package: JEL
Title: Jointly Estimated Landmarking for Dynamic Survival Prediction
Version: 2.2
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jinwoo", "Cho", email = "jinoojwcho@pitt.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Kehui", "Chen", role = "aut"))
Description: Dynamic prediction of survival outcomes from noisy longitudinal
    biomarkers using the Jointly Estimated Landmarking (JEL) approach. A local
    linear approximation summarises each biomarker trajectory around a landmark
    time by its recent level (intercept) and change (slope), and a flexible
    transformation survival model relates these summaries to the conditional
    risk. The package supports time-varying association functions via B-splines
    and multiple longitudinal processes through a fast EM algorithm, and provides
    dynamic prediction with time-dependent AUC and prediction-error evaluation.
    See Cho and Chen (2024) for methodological details.
